## Multi-tenancy

This portal is multi-tenant (wired by the `add-tenancy` skill).

- **Isolation driver:** `<database | row>`.
- **Engine:** `stancl/tenancy ^3.10`, identified by tenant **slug** (web) and a
  `tenant_id` token claim (MCP).
- **Framework binding:** `app/Support/StanclTenantResolver.php` fills
  `Mortel\Contracts\TenantResolver`; `mortelos/framework` is a composer
  `suggest`, bound only when installed.
- **Roles & policies:** owner-editable DB data, deny-by-default, gated through
  `App\Contracts\GovernanceGate` (`config('starter.governance.access_resolver')`).
- **Switcher:** shown only to users who belong to more than one tenant.
<!-- row driver only — keep this line, it is the one-way door: -->
- **⚠ Foreclosure (row driver):** this portal uses row-scoped isolation. It
  **cannot adopt `mortelos/framework` operate-mode** (database-per-tenant only)
  without migrating every scoped table into per-tenant databases. Shared
  (un-scoped) tables: `<users, ...>`.

### Tenant lifecycle (database driver)

```bash
php artisan tenants:migrate      # run database/migrations/tenant on every tenant DB
php artisan tenants:seed
php artisan tenants:run "<cmd>"   # run a command in each tenant context
```

Creating a `Tenant` row provisions its database automatically (stancl events);
deleting drops it. Never create tenant databases by hand.
